1. Locate each FROM declaration. If it ends with AS TABLE[...], confirm that the
   very next token after ] is ;, even when the next operation starts on a new line.
2. Confirm that FROM without AS TABLE, SOURCE, SINK and TO declarations also end
   with ;. Do not put ; between a connector and its AS TABLE schema.
3. Operation bodies contain semicolon-terminated statements, but their closing }
   has no additional semicolon. Return only the complete program.

